BT /F1 13 Tf 72 750 Td 15 TL (40 CFR 141.80\(c\) - action levels and percentile \(excerpts\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 728 Td 12 TL
(\(c\) Lead and copper action levels and method for determining whether there is an exceedance) Tj T*
(of the action level. Action levels must be determined based on tap water samples that must) Tj T*
(be considered for inclusion under 141.86\(e\).) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(1\) The lead action level is exceeded if the 90th percentile concentration of lead as) Tj T*
(specified in paragraph \(c\)\(3\) of this section is greater than 0.010 mg/L.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(2\) The copper action level is exceeded if the 90th percentile concentration of copper as) Tj T*
(specified in paragraph \(c\)\(3\) of this section is greater than 1.3 mg/L.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(3\) For purposes of this subpart, the 90th percentile concentration must be derived as) Tj T*
(follows. The results of all lead or copper samples taken during a tap sampling period must) Tj T*
(be placed in ascending order from the sample with the lowest concentration to the sample) Tj T*
(with the highest concentration. Each sampling result must be assigned a number, in ascending) Tj T*
(order beginning with the number 1 for the sample with the lowest concentration. The number) Tj T*
(assigned to the sample with the highest concentration must be equal to the total number of) Tj T*
(samples taken.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(B\) The number of samples taken during the tap sampling period must be multiplied by 0.9.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(C\) The 90th percentile concentration is the concentration in the numbered sample yielded) Tj T*
(after multiplying the number of samples by 0.9.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(D\) For water systems that collect five samples per tap sampling period, the 90th percentile) Tj T*
(concentration is the average of the highest and second highest concentration from the) Tj T*
(results in paragraph \(c\)\(3\)\(i\)\(A\) of this section.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(E\) For a water system that is allowed by the State to collect fewer than five samples in) Tj T*
(accordance with 141.86\(a\)\(2\) or has failed to meet their required minimum number of samples) Tj T*
(and collected fewer than five samples, the sample result with the highest concentration from) Tj T*
(the results in paragraph \(c\)\(3\)\(i\)\(A\) of this section is considered the 90th percentile) Tj T*
(value.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
