BT /F1 13 Tf 72 750 Td 15 TL (40 CFR 141.86\(a\)-\(e\) - tap site tiers and sampling \(excerpts\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 728 Td 12 TL
(\(a\) Selection of sampling sites. Tier 1 sampling sites consist of single family structures) Tj T*
(with lead service lines or copper pipes with lead solder installed after 1982. Tier 2 sites) Tj T*
(consist of buildings with similar plumbing materials. Tier 3 sites consist of single family) Tj T*
(structures with copper pipes with lead solder installed before 1983. Systems must use Tier 1) Tj T*
(sites when available.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Copper tiering keys on copper pipe with lead solder. A site may therefore carry a lead tier) Tj T*
(that differs from its copper tier, and eligibility is evaluated separately for each) Tj T*
(contaminant.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(b\) Sequential sampling at sites with lead service lines. At a site where the State has) Tj T*
(approved sequential sampling, the compliance sample for lead is the fifth liter drawn after) Tj T*
(stagnation. The first liter is informational only and is not used for compliance when a) Tj T*
(required pair is present. When only one liter of a required pair is present the site is) Tj T*
(excluded. Sequential sampling applies to lead only. Copper at these sites is reported as a) Tj T*
(single sample and is not subject to the pair rule.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(c\) Numbers of samples. The table below gives the required minimum number of samples by) Tj T*
(population served under standard monitoring and under reduced monitoring. Population-served) Tj T*
(changes move a system across minimum-count rows mid-record where applicable.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
