BT /F1 13 Tf 72 750 Td 15 TL (State guidance worked example - five-sample averaging) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 728 Td 12 TL
(Nevada Division of Environmental Protection, Bureau of Safe Drinking Water, Guidance for) Tj T*
(Small Water Systems, Section V, Example 2. Ordered lead results in mg/L: 0.008, 0.009,) Tj T*
(0.010, 0.013, 0.016.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Guidance text: If five samples are required: 5 x 0.9 = 4.5. The average of the 4th and 5th) Tj T*
(highest sample value reported is the 90th percentile. Computation: \(0.013 + 0.016\) / 2 =) Tj T*
(0.0145 mg/L, which the document reports as below the then-current lead action level of 0.015) Tj T*
(mg/L.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The same document restates the rule: in situations in which only 5 samples are taken, the) Tj T*
(average of the two with the highest levels is taken to determine the 90th percentile level.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
endstream
